# URLs the weekly outbound link check (.github/workflows/links.yml) skips.
# One regular expression per line, matched against the full URL. Every entry
# says why; "blocks bots" means it answers a link checker with 403/999 or a
# challenge page whatever the link's real state, so a check there can only
# ever be noise. Those links are not verified by anything — check them by hand
# when a page that cites them changes. Probed with lychee's user agent on
# 2026-11-24 unless noted.

# Rate-limit or block crawlers by policy (named in the lane brief, 2026-11-24).
^https?://([a-z0-9-]+\.)*linkedin\.com([/:?#]|$)
^https?://(www\.)?x\.com([/:?#]|$)
^https?://([a-z0-9-]+\.)*twitter\.com([/:?#]|$)
^https?://([a-z0-9-]+\.)*glassdoor\.[a-z.]+([/:?#]|$)

# Cloudflare challenge (cf-mitigated: challenge, 403) even for a browser user agent.
^https?://(www\.)?prachub\.com([/:?#]|$)
^https?://(www\.)?leetcode\.com([/:?#]|$)
^https?://support\.codesignal\.com([/:?#]|$)

# 403 to the link checker's user agent, 200 to a browser (probed 2026-11-24, run
# 45459520263: all 7 errors of the first run were teamblind.com posts cited as
# sources on the Amazon, Meta and Capital One pages). We respect the block
# rather than spoof a browser agent.
^https?://(www\.)?teamblind\.com([/:?#]|$)

# Akamai 403 to non-browser clients, browser user agent included.
^https?://dev\.mysql\.com([/:?#]|$)

# Bare origins used only for <link rel="preconnect">: the origin itself is a 404 by design.
^https://fonts\.googleapis\.com/?$
^https://fonts\.gstatic\.com/?$

# Microsoft Clarity's loader prefix, built in an inline script — not a link.
^https://www\.clarity\.ms/tag/?$
